# .gitattributes: the checkout may not rewrite the bytes this repository stores.
#
# Ticket: ORI-T-0082. Spec: spec/CI_CD.md section 1 (gate 9, the citation gate).
#
# GitHub's Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true. Without this file
# every text file arrives there with \r\n where the committed bytes have \n,
# and this repository holds three kinds of file for which that is not a
# cosmetic difference:
#
#   methodology/sections.json
#       A generated artifact. The staleness test in
#       crates/ori-gates/src/sections.rs compares it byte for byte against a
#       fresh parse, and the generator writes \n. A checkout that rewrites it
#       makes the file differ from its own generator on Windows alone.
#
#   methodology/AICD_Methodology_v0.3.html
#       The index records the document's length in bytes so that `wc -c` is a
#       staleness check a human can run. That only holds while the checkout
#       does not add a carriage return to each of its 1519 lines.
#
#   scripts/*.sh
#       A shell script whose shebang line ends \r\n is not executable, and a
#       `[ "$x" = passed ]` compared against a value read from a \r\n file is
#       never equal.
#
# This file is not the fix for the parser, and must not be read as one. The
# parser folds CRLF to LF itself (Index::parse, via lf_line_endings), so a
# document handed to it from anywhere at all produces one index. That is proved
# by a_crlf_document_indexes_identically_to_the_same_document_with_lf, which
# builds its CRLF document in memory and never consults git. What this file
# fixes is the part no parser can reach: a generated file compared byte for
# byte, and a script handed to a shell.
#
# One rule rather than a list of paths. A list says nothing about the next file
# someone adds, and the invariant wanted here is not "these three files" but
# "the working tree is the bytes the repository stores, on every platform".
# text=auto leaves anything git detects as binary alone; eol=lf checks text out
# with \n everywhere, Windows included.
* text=auto eol=lf
